# Patch:        020-extraction-roots
# Phase:        pre
# Target:       multilinear-util/src/hax_roots.rs, multilinear-util/src/lib.rs
# Hunks:        2
# Class:        bound
# Gap:          docs/extractor-issues.md 4 (aeneas drops a method that no free
#               function calls). Both rooted items are associated functions
#               of `Point`.
# Cost:         none in a normal build: the module exists only under
#               cfg(hax_backend_lean). In the extracted variant it adds free
#               functions, each of which calls one item of the crate.
#               No existing body changes.
# Upstreamable: no: the module exists only for the extractor.
# Drop when:    charon orders `--start-from` methods, so that the methods
#               themselves can be roots.
# Test:         lint p3-multilinear-util unexpected_cfgs
# Mutation:     the module is gated on a misspelled cfg, so a normal
#               `cargo check` reports `unexpected_cfgs`.
#
# The roots are:
#
# - the equality polynomial of two points, the product over i of p_i q_i + (1 - p_i)(1 - q_i);
# - the point constructor, which brings the point type into the model for the crates that store points.
#
# Two sibling evaluations are not rooted:
#
# - the selection polynomial's closure updates a captured variable, whose back function CoreModels cannot take (docs/extractor-issues.md 60);
# - the successor polynomial walks a zip of two slices backwards, and CoreModels has no model of that walk.
#
# The fields stay generic, so the Lean model quantifies over every implementation.
#
